{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:68:1","rows":[{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبو بكر والمفضل وهبيرة وورش وابن محيصن وابن عامر والكسائي ويعقوب","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Bakr, al-Mufaḍḍal, Hubayra, Warsh, Ibn Muḥayṣin, Ibn ʿĀmir, al-Kisāʾī, and Yaʿqūb assimilate the second nūn in the spelled name into wāw.","anchor":"أدغم النون الثانية في هجائها في الواو أبو بكر والمفضل وهبيرة وورش وابن محيصن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الباقون","stance":"reports","claim":"The remaining readers pronounce the nūn distinctly.","anchor":"والباقون بالإظهار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عيسى بن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿĪsā ibn ʿUmar reads nūn with fatḥa, as though an implicit verb governs it.","anchor":"وقرأ عيسى بن عمر بفتحها كأنه أضمر فعلا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"ابن عباس ونصر وابن أبي إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās, Naṣr, and Ibn Abī Isḥāq read it with kasra, supplied by an implicit oath preposition.","anchor":"وقرأ ابن عباس ونصر وابن أبي إسحاق بكسرها على إضمار حرف القسم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"هارون ومحمد ابن السميقع","stance":"reports","claim":"Hārūn and Muḥammad ibn al-Sumayqiʿ read it with ḍamma as a built form.","anchor":"وقرأ هارون ومحمد ابن السميقع بضمها على البناء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"معاوية بن قرة عن أبيه","stance":"reports","claim":"A report from Muʿāwiya ibn Qurra, raised through his father to the Prophet, says nūn is a tablet of light.","anchor":"فروى معاوية بن قرة عن أبيه يرفعه إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال ن لوح من نور","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ثابت البناني","stance":"reports","claim":"Thābit al-Bunānī says nūn is the inkwell; al-Ḥasan and Qatāda share this view.","anchor":"وروى ثابت البناني أن ن الدواة وقاله الحسن وقتادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو هريرة عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"A lengthy report says God created the pen, then nūn as its inkwell, ordered the pen to write all events through the Resurrection, and sealed it; He then created the intellect and said He would perfect it in those He loved and diminish it in those He hated. The most intelligent are most obedient.","anchor":"عن أبي هريرة قال سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول أول ما خلق الله القلم ثم خلق النون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid says nūn is the whale beneath the seventh earth and the pen is the one that wrote the Reminder.","anchor":"وعن مجاهد قال ن الحوت الذي تحت الأرض السابعة قال والقلم الذي كتب به الذكر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"مقاتل ومرة الهمداني وعطاء الخراساني والسدي والكلبي","stance":"reports","claim":"Muqātil, Murra al-Hamdānī, ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī, al-Suddī, and al-Kalbī say nūn is the whale that bears the earths.","anchor":"وكذا قال مقاتل ومرة الهمداني وعطاء الخراساني والسدي والكلبي إن النون هو الحوت","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Ẓabyān transmits from Ibn ʿAbbās that the pen first wrote what would be, water vapor rose and formed heaven, then the whale bore the earth; when it shook, mountains fixed it, and the mountains boast over earth.","anchor":"وروى أبو ظبيان عن ابن عباس قال أول ما خلق الله القلم فجرى بما هو كائن","mentions":[]}]} 
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:68:1#2","rows":[{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الكلبي ومقاتل","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kalbī and Muqātil say the whale's name is al-Bahmūt.","anchor":"وقال الكلبي ومقاتل اسمه البهموت","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الراجز","stance":"reports","claim":"The rajaz poet's lines name the whale al-Bahmūt, attesting that name.","anchor":"قال الراجز مالي أراكم كلكم سكوتا والله ربي خلق البهموتا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"أبو اليقظان والواقدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū al-Yaqẓān and al-Wāqidī call the whale Layūthā.","anchor":"وقال أبو اليقظان والواقدي ليوثا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"كعب","stance":"reports","claim":"Kaʿb gives the whale's name as Lawthūthā, then also reports the name Balhamūthā.","anchor":"وقال كعب لوثوثا قال بلهموثا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"كعب","stance":"reports","claim":"Kaʿb recounts that Satan whispered to the whale bearing the earths, and it considered casting them off; God sent a creature into its nostril and brain, the whale complained, and God let the creature out, whereupon it ceased its plan.","anchor":"قال كعب إن إبليس تغلغل إلى الحوت الذي على ظهره الأرضون فوسوس في قلبه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"الضحاك عن ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk, reporting from Ibn ʿAbbās, says nūn is the final letter of the name al-Raḥmān; alif-lām-rā, ḥā-mīm, and nūn are its separate letters.","anchor":"وقال الضحاك عن ابن عباس إن ن آخر حرف من حروف الرحمن قال الر وحم ون الرحمن تعالى متقطعة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن زيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Zayd says nūn is an object by which God swears.","anchor":"وقال ابن زيد هو قسم أقسم الله تعالى به","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن كيسان","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Kaysān says nūn opens the sūra.","anchor":"وقال ابن كيسان هو فاتحة السورة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view treats nūn as the name of the sūra.","anchor":"وقيل اسم السورة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"عطاء وأبو العالية","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAṭāʾ and Abū al-ʿĀliya say nūn opens names of God such as Naṣīr, Nūr, and Nāṣir.","anchor":"وقال عطاء وأبو العالية هو افتتاح اسمه نصير ونور وناصر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"محمد بن كعب","stance":"reports","claim":"Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb says God swore by His support of believers, a true promise supported by 30:47.","anchor":"وقال محمد بن كعب أقسم الله تعالى بنصره للمؤمنين وهو حق","mentions":["30:47"]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"جعفر الصادق","stance":"reports","claim":"Jaʿfar al-Ṣādiq says nūn is a river of Paradise called Nūn.","anchor":"وقال جعفر الصادق هو نهر من أنهار الجنة يقال له نون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["نٓ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"القشيري أبو نصر عبد الرحيم","stance":"prefers","claim":"Al-Qushayrī prefers taking nūn as the familiar alphabet letter: it is uninflected, whereas a full word would inflect like al-qalam, and so resembles other sūra initials; on this view it names the sūra.","anchor":"وهو اختيار القشيري أبو نصر عبد الرحيم في تفسيره قال لأن ن حرف لم يعرب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God swears by the pen because it conveys meaning like the tongue; the oath encompasses every writing pen in heaven and earth.","anchor":"أقسم بالقلم لما فيه من البيان كاللسان وهو واقع على كل قلم مما يكتب به","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو الفتح البستي","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū al-Fatḥ al-Bustī's poem contrasts the sword with the pen and says God's oath gives the scribal pen lasting honor and distinction.","anchor":"ومنه قول أبي الفتح البستي إذا أقسم الأبطال يوما بسيفهم وعدوه مما يكسب المجد والكرم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās says this is an oath by God's created, luminous pen, as long as the distance between heaven and earth, which wrote everything destined until Resurrection on the Preserved Tablet.","anchor":"وقال ابن عباس هذا قسم بالقلم الذي خلقه الله فأمره فجرى بكتابة جميع ما هو كائن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Another account from Ibn ʿAbbās says God split the pen in two, ordered it to write, and told it to record what would happen until Resurrection.","anchor":"ويقال خلق الله القلم ثم نظر إليه فانشق نصفين فقال اجر فقال يا رب بم أجري","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"الوليد بن عبادة بن الصامت","stance":"reports","claim":"On his deathbed, al-Walīd ibn ʿUbāda ibn al-Ṣāmit says his father urged him to fear God, believe in divine oneness and predestination, then cited a Prophetic report about the pen.","anchor":"وقال الوليد بن عبادة بن الصامت أوصاني أبي عند موته فقال يا بني اتق الله واعلم","mentions":[]}]} 
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:68:1-3","rows":[{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم","stance":"reports","claim":"The Prophetic report cited by al-Walīd ibn ʿUbāda says the first created thing was the pen; God told it to write destiny, and it wrote what had happened and would happen forever.","anchor":"إن أول ما خلق الله القلم فقال له اكتب فقال يا رب وما أكتب فقال اكتب القدر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās says the first created pen wrote everything that would be, including the words “May the hands of Abū Lahab perish” (111:1).","anchor":"وقال ابن عباس أول ما خلق الله القلم فأمره أن يكتب ما هو كائن فكتب فيما كتب تبت يدا أبي لهب","mentions":["111:1"]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda says the pen is a blessing from God to His servants.","anchor":"وقال قتادة القلم نعمة من الله تعالى على عباده","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَٱلْقَلَمِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"غيره","stance":"reports","claim":"Another account distinguishes the first pen, which wrote destiny in the Reminder and was placed above the Throne, from a second pen for earthly writing, discussed at 96:1.","anchor":"قال غيره فخلق الله القلم الأول فكتب ما يكون في الذكر ووضعه عنده فوق عرشه","mentions":["96:1"]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Mā yasṭurūn means what they write.","anchor":"قوله تعالى وما يسطرون أي وما يكتبون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās says the writers meant are angels recording the deeds of human beings.","anchor":"يريد الملائكة يكتبون أعمال بني آدم قاله ابن عباس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view takes the writers to be people, writing and communicating with one another.","anchor":"وقيل وما يكتبون أي الناس ويتفاهمون به","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās also explains mā yasṭurūn as “what they know.”","anchor":"وقال ابن عباس ومعنى وما يسطرون وما يعلمون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:1"],"words":["مَا يَسْطُرُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Mā may be a relative pronoun or a verbal noun, yielding “what they write” or “their writing”; the referent may be any writers or the recording angels.","anchor":"وما موصولة أو مصدرية أي ومسطوراتهم أو وسطرهم ويراد به كل من يسطر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:2"],"words":["مَآ أَنتَ بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ بِمَجْنُونٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This is the oath's answer, refuting the polytheists' claim that the Prophet was insane and possessed by a devil; compare 15:6.","anchor":"هذا جواب القسم وهو نفي وكان المشركون يقولون للنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم إنه مجنون به شيطان","mentions":["15:6"]},{"verses":["68:2"],"words":["بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Here niʿma means God's mercy.","anchor":"أي برحمة ربك والنعمة ههنا الرحمة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:2"],"words":["بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alternatively, the phrase is an oath: “By your Lord's favor, you are not mad,” since both wāw and bāʾ can mark an oath.","anchor":"ويحتمل ثانيا أن النعمة ههنا قسم وتقديره ما أنت ونعمة ربك بمجنون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:2"],"words":["بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another analysis reads the statement as “You are not mad, and praise belongs to God.”","anchor":"وقيل هو كما تقول ما أنت بمجنون والحمد لله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:2"],"words":["بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A further analysis takes it to mean “You are not mad, and the favor belongs to your Lord,” like the expression “Glory and praise be to You, O God.”","anchor":"وقيل معناه ما أنت بمجنون والنعمة لربك كقولهم سبحانك اللهم وبحمدك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:2"],"words":["بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"لبيد والنابغة","stance":"reports","claim":"The quoted lines of Labīd and al-Nābigha illustrate supplying an understood “he is” in a coordinated phrase.","anchor":"ومنه قول لبيد وأفردت في الدنيا بفقد عشيرتي وفارقني جار بأربد نافع أي وهو أربد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:2"],"words":["بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The prepositional phrase attaches to the negated “mad,” as it would to an affirmed predicate; its accusative role is circumstantial, meaning he is not mad while favored by God.","anchor":"والباء في بنعمة ربك متعلقة بمجنون منفيا كما يتعلق بغافل مثبتا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:3"],"words":["غَيْرُ مَمْنُونٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Prophet's reward is neither cut off nor diminished; Arabic manantu al-ḥabl means “I cut the rope,” and ḥabl manīn is weak.","anchor":"غير مقطوع ولا منقوص يقال مننت الحبل إذا قطعته وحبل منين إذا كان غير متين","mentions":[]}]} 
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:68:4","rows":[{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["وَإِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس ومجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās and Mujāhid say the Prophet follows a great religion, none more beloved or pleasing to God.","anchor":"قال ابن عباس ومجاهد على خلق على دين عظيم من الأديان ليس دين أحب إلى الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عائشة","stance":"reports","claim":"In Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim, ʿĀʾisha says the Prophet's character was the Qur'an.","anchor":"وفي صحيح مسلم عن عائشة أن خلقه كان القرآن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"علي وعطية","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAlī and ʿAṭiyya interpret it as the manners taught by the Qur'an.","anchor":"وقال علي وعطية هو أدب القرآن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation is the Prophet's gentleness toward his community and his honoring of them.","anchor":"وقيل هو رفقه بأمته وإكرامه إياهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda says it is the Prophet's practice of obeying God's commands and avoiding His prohibitions.","anchor":"وقال قتادة هو ما كان يأتمر به من أمر الله وينتهى عنه مما نهى الله عنه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view understands it as a noble disposition; al-Māwardī calls this the apparent meaning.","anchor":"وقيل أي إنك على طبع كريم الماوردي وهو الظاهر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Khuluq is the etiquette a person cultivates until it becomes like part of his nature; khaym is innate temperament, and khaym also names a mountain.","anchor":"وحقيقة الخلق في اللغة هو ما يأخذ به الإنسان نفسه من الأدب يسمى خلقا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The kasra form khaym denotes innate disposition, unlike cultivated khuluq; al-Aʿshā's poem illustrates traits returning to their natural state.","anchor":"وأما ما طبع عليه من الأدب فهو الخيم بالكسر السجية والطبيعة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الأعشى","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Aʿshā's verse uses khaym for natural disposition, showing that character returns to its innate habits.","anchor":"وقد أوضح الأعشى ذلك في شعره وإذا ذو الفضول ضن على المولى وعادت لخيمها الأخلاق","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["وَإِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عائشة","stance":"reports","claim":"Asked about the Prophet's character, ʿĀʾisha recited the first ten verses of Sūrat al-Muʾminūn; no one had better character, and whoever called him from among Companions or family heard him answer “At your service.”","anchor":"وسئلت أيضا عن خلقه عليه السلام فقرأت قد أفلح المؤمنون إلى عشر آيات","mentions":["23:1","23:2","23:3","23:4","23:5","23:6","23:7","23:8","23:9","23:10"]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["وَإِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"prefers","claim":"Al-Qurṭubī says ʿĀʾisha's explanation in Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim is the soundest view; the Prophet possessed the fullest share of every praiseworthy character.","anchor":"قلت ما ذكرته عن عائشة في صحيح مسلم أصح الأقوال ولم يذكر خلق محمود إلا وكان للنبي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"inward","speaker":"الجنيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Junayd says the Prophet's character is called great because he had no aspiration apart from God.","anchor":"وقال الجنيد سمي خلقه عظيما لأنه لم تكن له همة سوى الله تعالى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another explanation says his character is great because it gathers noble qualities, supported by the report that God sent him to perfect noble character.","anchor":"وقيل سمي خلقه عظيما لاجتماع مكارم الأخلاق فيه يدل عليه قوله عليه السلام إن الله بعثني لأتمم مكارم الأخلاق","mentions":[]},{"verses":["68:4"],"words":["خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Another explanation ties his great character to carrying out God's instruction in 7:199; a report says God trained him well through that command, and after he accepted it declared him of great character.","anchor":"وقيل لأنه امتثل تأديب الله تعالى إياه بقوله تعالى خذ العفو وأمر بالعرف وأعرض عن الجاهلين","mentions":["7:199"]}]}

